  "slug": "visual-activity-hierarchical-2c1b",
  "summary": "Recent preprints test whether normative denoising models and thalamocortical circuit models reproduce behavioral and neural history effects.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is computational modeling of how past information shapes present neural processing and behavior. A recurrent autoencoder trained to denoise videos spontaneously reproduces human serial dependence in orientation judgments. A circuit model of thalamocortical PUL-PPC replay shows how history signals are reconstructed and redirect later decisions. A review of normative and neural network models of multisensory integration adds comparative equations and Python code. The items differ in scope, so this is the dominant thread rather than a shared finding. What is new is that serial dependence emerges from a normative denoising objective, and that history is traced to a specific thalamocortical pathway.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
